    {
      "fn": "VFX_ComposeSweptTrail",
      "label": "SWEPT TRAIL",
      "category": "metal",
      "type": "continuous",
      "_comment": "H1 bench. ONE trail, one style — a primary is judged ALONE or a bad result has two candidate causes. Set swept_style in the block below by hand to compare styles. The HAZE + RIBBON pairing now lives in the PROJECTILE entry, where it belongs.",
      "draw_block": [
        "{",
        "static Matrix sweptXf;",
        "static int sweptH = -1;",
        "static float sweptPrevT = -1.0f;",
        "float a = $TIME * 2.4f;",
        "Vector3 p = Vector3Add($POS, (Vector3){ 3.0f * sinf(a), 1.7f + 0.45f * sinf(a * 0.7f), 2.1f * cosf(a) });",
        "if ($TIME < sweptPrevT) { VFX_KillSweptTrail(sweptH); sweptH = -1; }",
        "sweptPrevT = $TIME;",
        "sweptXf = MatrixTranslate(p.x, p.y, p.z);",
        "if (sweptH < 0) sweptH = VFX_ComposeSweptTrail(&sweptXf, VC_MAT_WATER, 1.60f, 0.85f, VFX_TRAIL_RIBBON);",
        "}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "fn": "VFX_ComposeSweptTrail",
      "label": "TRAIL HAZE",
      "category": "water",
      "type": "continuous",
      "_comment": "The HAZE style ALONE. It is deliberately faint, so on its own it should read as a wide soft wedge, widest where it meets the emitter and coming to a point behind — NOT as a bright ribbon. If it is invisible here, raise swept_alpha; if it looks like a ribbon, the triangle curve is wrong.",
      "draw_block": [
        "{",
        "static Matrix hazeXf;",
        "static int hazeH = -1;",
        "static float hazePrevT = -1.0f;",
        "float a = $TIME * 2.4f;",
        "Vector3 p = Vector3Add($POS, (Vector3){ 3.0f * sinf(a), 1.7f + 0.45f * sinf(a * 0.7f), 2.1f * cosf(a) });",
        "if ($TIME < hazePrevT) { VFX_KillSweptTrail(hazeH); hazeH = -1; }",
        "hazePrevT = $TIME;",
        "hazeXf = MatrixTranslate(p.x, p.y, p.z);",
        "if (hazeH < 0) hazeH = VFX_ComposeSweptTrail(&hazeXf, VC_MAT_WATER, 2.40f, 0.85f, VFX_TRAIL_HAZE);",
        "}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "fn": "VFX_ComposeGroundWave",
      "label": "GROUND WAVE",
      "category": "earth",
      "type": "continuous",
      "_comment": "H2 bench. Loops a 1.6 s shockwave so the expansion, the leading crest and the fade are all visible without re-triggering. Uses VFX_GroundHeightFromMap, NOT NULL: the first version passed NULL 'because the sandbox floor is flat', which on a heightmap map draws a FLAT ring that happens to sit on the ground where the ground is level and floats or sinks everywhere else — i.e. the bench could not show the one thing H2 exists to do.",
      "draw_call": "VFX_ComposeGroundWave($POS, VC_MAT_EARTH, 5.0f, fmodf($TIME, 1.6f) / 1.6f, VFX_GroundHeightFromMap, NULL)"
    },
    {
      "fn": "VFX_ComposeImpactFlash",
      "label": "IMPACT FLASH",
      "category": "util",
      "type": "oneshot",
      "_comment": "Impact primary, benched ALONE. The decal beat inside VFX_ComposeImpactPackage shipped dead (no texture in .ud) and nobody noticed for a month because it had no bench entry of its own — a primary that cannot be fired on its own cannot be seen to be missing.",
      "trigger_call": "VFX_ComposeImpactFlash($POS, VC_MAT_FIRE, 1.0f, 0.8f)"
    },
    {
      "fn": "VFX_ComposeImpactDistort",
      "label": "IMPACT DISTORT",
      "category": "util",
      "type": "oneshot",
      "_comment": "Impact primary, benched ALONE. The decal beat inside VFX_ComposeImpactPackage shipped dead (no texture in .ud) and nobody noticed for a month because it had no bench entry of its own — a primary that cannot be fired on its own cannot be seen to be missing.",
      "trigger_call": "VFX_ComposeImpactDistort($POS, 1.0f, 0.8f)"
    },
    {
      "fn": "VFX_ComposeImpactDecal",
      "label": "IMPACT DECAL",
      "category": "util",
      "type": "oneshot",
      "_comment": "Impact primary, benched ALONE. The decal beat inside VFX_ComposeImpactPackage shipped dead (no texture in .ud) and nobody noticed for a month because it had no bench entry of its own — a primary that cannot be fired on its own cannot be seen to be missing.",
      "trigger_call": "VFX_ComposeImpactDecal($POS, VC_MAT_FIRE, 1.0f, 0.8f)"
    },
    {
      "fn": "VFX_ComposeSparkTrail",
      "label": "SPARK TRAIL",
      "category": "util",
      "type": "continuous",
      "_comment": "Benched as ONE spark on a loop, not a swarm. The first version emitted 40/s and the owner could only see 'a pile of strands' — a primary has to be judgeable alone before it is judgeable in a crowd.",
      "draw_block": [
        "{",
        "static float acc = 0.0f;",
        "acc += GetFrameTime();",
        "if (acc > 0.55f) {",
        "    acc = 0.0f;",
        "    Vector3 c = Vector3Add($POS, (Vector3){0.0f, 1.2f, 0.0f});",
        "    float ang = $TIME * 1.3f;",
        "    Vector3 sp = (Vector3){ c.x + cosf(ang) * 2.0f, c.y, c.z + sinf(ang) * 2.0f };",
        "    Vector3 v = Vector3Scale(Vector3Normalize(Vector3Subtract(c, sp)), 3.0f);",
        "    VFX_ComposeSparkTrail(sp, Vector3Add(v, (Vector3){ -sinf(ang) * 2.2f, 0.4f, cosf(ang) * 2.2f }), VC_MAT_LIGHTNING, 0.5f, 0.9f);",
        "}",
        "}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "fn": "VFX_ComposeProjectile",
      "label": "PROJECTILE",
      "category": "water",
      "type": "continuous",
      "_comment": "COMPOSITE. Orb + haze field + main tail + 2 spiralling wisps, flying a long curved path so the wisps' spiral and the field's lag are both visible. Killed and respawned on re-trigger because the bench clock jumps backwards.",
      "draw_block": [
        "{",
        "static Matrix projXf;",
        "static int projH = -1;",
        "static float projPrevT = -1.0f;",
        "if ($TIME < projPrevT) { VFX_KillProjectile(projH); projH = -1; }",
        "projPrevT = $TIME;",
        "float a = $TIME * 1.5f;",
        "Vector3 p = Vector3Add($POS, (Vector3){ 4.0f * sinf(a), 1.8f + 0.6f * sinf(a * 0.8f), 3.0f * cosf(a * 0.7f) });",
        "projXf = MatrixTranslate(p.x, p.y, p.z);",
        "if (projH < 0) projH = VFX_ComposeProjectile(&projXf, VC_MAT_WATER, 0.34f);",
        "}"
      ]
    }
  ],
